BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 785.89 Td (the database by itself and it cannot execute SQL. The backend validates all generated SQL) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 769.39 Td (before execution.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13.5 Tf 50.00 736.89 Td (What RAG Means) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 707.89 Td (RAG means Retrieval-Augmented Generation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 684.39 Td (In simple words:) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.3 Tf 60.00 655.89 Td (Retrieve trusted information first.) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.3 Tf 60.00 644.39 Td (Then generate an answer using only that retrieved information.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 620.89 Td (Without RAG, an LLM may answer from general training knowledge and may hallucinate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 604.39 Td (Hallucination means the model invents information that is not supported by real data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 580.89 Td (With RAG, the system first retrieves relevant records from PostgreSQL, then asks the LLM to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 564.39 Td (explain those records. Therefore, the final answer is grounded in the user's own health) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 547.89 Td (data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 524.39 Td (In this project, the RAG flow is:) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.3 Tf 60.00 495.89 Td (User question) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.3 Tf 60.00 484.39 Td (-> ML-service converts question to SQL) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.3 Tf 60.00 472.89 Td (-> Backend validates SQL) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.3 Tf 60.00 461.39 Td (-> Backend retrieves user-specific records from PostgreSQL) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.3 Tf 60.00 449.89 Td (-> Sensitive values are redacted) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.3 Tf 60.00 438.39 Td (-> ML-service generates a final answer from retrieved rows) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.3 Tf 60.00 426.89 Td (-> Backend saves the conversation) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.3 Tf 60.00 415.39 Td (-> Frontend displays the assistant response) Tj ET
BT /F2 13.5 Tf 50.00 382.89 Td (Main Technical Terms) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 353.89 Td (LLM: Large Language Model. A model that understands and generates human language. In this) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 337.39 Td (system it helps understand questions, generate SQL, and write friendly answers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 313.89 Td (RAG: Retrieval-Augmented Generation. A pattern where the system retrieves trusted data first) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 297.39 Td (and then uses an LLM to generate an answer from that data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 273.89 Td (NL2SQL: Natural Language to SQL. The process of converting a user question into a SQL query.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 250.39 Td (SQL: Structured Query Language. The language used to read records from PostgreSQL.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 226.89 Td (PostgreSQL: The relational database that stores user records such as medicines, routines,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 210.39 Td (medication status events, allergy cards, mood logs, caregiver alerts, and assistant) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 193.89 Td (messages.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 170.39 Td (Schema digest: A controlled description of the database tables and columns that the LLM is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 153.89 Td (allowed to use. It prevents the LLM from guessing unknown or unsafe tables.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 130.39 Td (Intent: The detected purpose of the message. Example intents include missed medications, low) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 113.89 Td (stock, diabetes prediction, health advice, emotional support, or agentic action.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 90.39 Td (User scoping: A safety rule that every user-specific database query must include the current) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 50.00 73.89 Td (authenticated user id. In this codebase, the backend binds the logged-in user's id as $1.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 50.00 28 Td (Page 2 of 14) Tj ET
endstream
